From c8e14dbd41f757068aa05136bd4fc702c91eb67d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 19:51:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix broken install, image build, HTTP transport, and security
 gaps

The project did not work as the README described. This change makes the
documented Quick Start and security claims actually hold:

Structure & install
- Move the package (pyproject, src/, tests/, Dockerfile, example yaml)
  from the cli-mcp/ subdirectory to the repo root so
  'git clone && cd CLI-MCP && pip install .' works as documented
- Remove committed __pycache__/ and .egg-info/ artifacts; add .gitignore
- Fix placeholder URLs in pyproject.toml

Broken entry points
- 'cli-mcp --build-image' looked for the Dockerfile at src/Dockerfile
  and always failed; it now searches the CWD and the repo root
- HTTP mode crashed with TypeError: FastMCP.run() takes no host/port.
  It now serves the streamable-http app via uvicorn on the configured
  host/port
- The tools image failed to build on Ubuntu 24.04 (PEP 668
  externally-managed-environment); set PIP_BREAK_SYSTEM_PACKAGES and
  drop the failing pip self-upgrade. Also symlink fdfind -> fd

Security claims that were not implemented
- Timeout enforcement was dead code: asyncio.wait_for wrapped only
  process creation, so runaway commands hung forever. Timeouts now
  bound execution and kill the process
- The HTTP auth token was never checked; requests now require
  'Authorization: Bearer <token>' when CLI_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN is set, and
  the server warns loudly when it is not
- The 'rm -rf /' pattern only matched commands ending in '/'; harden it
  (flag order, --no-preserve-root) and un-anchor the fork-bomb pattern
- The blocklist was skipped entirely in allowlist mode; it now applies
  in every mode, and allowlist mode rejects shell chaining characters
  that would smuggle in disallowed tools

Bug fixes
- load_config shallow-copied DEFAULT_CONFIG, leaking mutations into the
  module-level defaults; use deepcopy
- Volume mount flags were built by splitting a string, breaking on
  paths with spaces; build argv lists instead
- normalize_path now converts Windows drive-letter paths on any
  platform (fixes the failing test)
- CLI_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN env override wrote the token value into the field
  holding the env var name; removed
- _coerce_value turned CLI_MCP_TIMEOUT=1 into True; parse ints first
- run_cli/run_script share one validated execution path; run_script no
  longer double-validates

Docs & CI
- README: fix clone path, project structure, env var table, auth and
  endpoint documentation, blocklist table, Docker deployment example
- Sync cli-mcp.example.yaml with the hardened defaults
- Add GitHub Actions CI (ruff + pytest on Python 3.10/3.12)
- Add tests: default blocklist coverage, allowlist chaining, timeout
  kill behavior, bearer auth middleware, config isolation (32 passing)

